  "selected_observable_guarantee": [
    "Each active endpoint consumes a FIFO queue and attempts one 512-byte record each 20 ms slot. Every record contains either one complete queued IP packet up to 488 bytes or dummy padding. New records are dropped on queue overflow at 64 packets; oversized packets are dropped. Late scheduling skips missed slots and restarts from current monotonic time.",
    "The actual MACsec controlled port encrypts/authenticates these records before the wire. Useful Inner-IPsec payloads cross the shim and are recovered at the peer. The bridge Outer Firewall accepts only 0x88e5. Physical-wire capture retains SCI/AN/PN/length and never emits ciphertext bodies.",
    "The six traffic controls include useful both ways, Inner-SA loss/restoration and Outer-MACsec loss/restoration. The first implementation exits on a normal ENETDOWN receive error during deliberate loss. The repaired receiver retains its TUN and handles that link error; final restoration succeeds. Send errors during intentional link loss remain visible.",
    "The finite idle/load/idle windows observe equal wire sizes and measured intervals. The configured 20 ms schedule is not a hard real-time guarantee. Host clock behavior, CPU scheduling, active-link availability and aggregate offered rate within capacity are assumptions. Queue behavior, link outages, endpoint start/stop, MAC addresses/SCI/PN and timing jitter remain observable.",
    "The implementation is a supplemental explicit MACsec-layer size/rate masking mechanism, not a conformant RFC 9347 AGGFRAG or IEEE 802.1AEdk implementation. Anti-jamming, physical interception prevention, full traffic-analysis security and product approval are not established."
  ]
}
